          equipment: "Two denominations of chips: 'Kan' and 'Mon' (1 Kan = 12 Mon typically).",
          dealing: "Deal cards to the 3 active players. Place cards face-up in the center (the 'field').",
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Score as close to 88 points as possible (the par score). Players pay/receive based on deviation from 88. Alternatively, form valuable yaku combinations to stop play early and claim payment.',
          gameplay: "1. Bidding Phase (if more than 3 players): Players bid to determine the 3 active players for the round. Non-active players sit out but may still earn from teyaku. 2. Dealing: Deal cards to the 3 active players. Place cards face-up in the center (the 'field'). 3. Playing Phase: Players take turns playing a card from hand to capture matching cards from the field. A card matches if it's from the same month/suit. After playing from hand, flip the top card from the deck. If it matches a field card, capture it. Captured cards go into the player's scoring pile. 4. Scoring: Total card points = 264 (par = 88 per player). Teyaku (Initial Hand Combinations): Declared before play for immediate payment. Deki-Yaku (Play Combinations): Formed during play. Player can stop early to claim payment. Final score = (Your points - 88). Positive = win, Negative = loss.",
          keyRules: [
            'The par score of 88 is key—aim to exceed it, not just maximize points.',
            'Teyaku are initial hand combinations declared before play for immediate payment.',
            'Deki-yaku are combinations formed during play; players can stop early to claim payment.',
            'Cards match by month/suit (same month cards capture each other).',
            'After playing from hand, flip top card from deck—if it matches field card, capture it.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Focus on capturing high-value cards (Brights, Animals, Ribbons). Avoid letting opponents form yaku.',
          intermediate: 'Track which cards have been played to anticipate remaining cards. Decide whether to stop early with a yaku or continue playing for more points.',
          advanced: 'Calculate exact point differentials. Bluff during bidding to become an active player. Memorize all yaku and their values to maximize scoring opportunities.',
          tips: [
            'The par score of 88 is key—aim to exceed it, not just maximize points.',
            'Stopping early with a yaku guarantees payment, but continuing might yield more.',
            "In the bidding phase, assess your hand's potential before committing.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
