          human: "Hachi-Hachi (八八, '88') is the most representative Japanese Hanafuda fishing game. The name refers to the par score of 88 points (one-third of the 264 total points in the deck). Played by 3-6 players with a bidding phase to determine the three active players each round. Features complex scoring with teyaku (initial hand combinations) and deki-yaku (combinations formed during play). Players can stop early if they form valuable combinations.",
